# mixdog-app-server-daemon compose_flip.rs real_core: the takeover owner, the card holds and the service
file: native/core/crates/mixdog-app-server-daemon/src/compose_flip.rs
place: in real_core, where `let human_only = Arc::new(...HumanOnlyLock::new(takeover_holds.clone()));` is built, directly after it add:
add:
    // The core's takeover owner (the engine's `TakeoverPort`, `takeover/ready`) and its holds for the cards it raises on the one human-only lock
    // (`item/browser/requestApproval`, a screen takeover, a secret request): read by the engine runner and the tool adapter (s4).
    let takeover = Arc::new(crate::takeover_port::CoreTakeover::new(takeover_holds.clone()));
    let card_holds = Arc::new(mixdog_core_session::session::secret_input::CardHolds::new(human_only.clone()));
place: `TakeoverGates::new(takeover_holds, human_only.clone())` moves `takeover_holds`: change it to `takeover_holds.clone()` (or place the two lines above before it).
place: after `builder.register(Arc::new(mixdog_core_session::session::secret_input::HumanOnlyService::new(human_only)))?;` (it moves `human_only`: the `card_holds` line above clones it first)
add:   builder.register(Arc::new(crate::takeover_port::TakeoverReadyService::new(takeover.clone())))?; // `takeover/ready`: the renderer reports a login takeover ready
note:  `takeover` (the TakeoverPort) is used by the registration; `card_holds` is taken by the browser engine wiring of s4-engine-runner / s4-tool-adapter, which calls hold_for_request_in when it raises item/browser/requestApproval and release on the answer and on serverRequest/resolved: add the `card_holds` line with that wiring if it is not in this wave (an unused binding is refused by the lint).

